    <!-- honesty panel -->
    <string name="lantools_honesty_title">Protocol Boundaries · HONESTY</string>
    <string name="lantools_honesty_line_1">fling-compatible semantics (fling 1.1-3): raw TCP byte stream — no length prefix, no checksum, no encryption; connection close (EOF) ends the transfer, one connection per transfer.</string>
    <string name="lantools_honesty_line_2">With port 0 the kernel assigns an ephemeral port; the ACTUAL LISTEN PORT must be given to the sender. Leaving this page stops receiving.</string>
    <string name="lantools_honesty_line_3">AP client isolation blocks devices on the same Wi-Fi from reaching each other; cross-subnet and hotspot-client traffic is usually unreachable too.</string>
    <string name="lantools_honesty_line_4">The sender targets the receiver LAN IP and port; public / NAT-ed addresses cannot connect directly.</string>
    <string name="lantools_honesty_line_5">The WOL magic packet is a 102-byte UDP broadcast with no acknowledgement; the target must have wake-on-LAN enabled in BIOS / firmware and stay on standby power.</string>
    <string name="lantools_honesty_line_6">This page fabricates nothing: unknown addresses, ports and byte counts show \"--\"; the log records only connections and transfers that actually happened.</string>
